## AdSense readiness

The public homepage is the only page configured to render Google-served ads.
Login, profile, and puzzle screens are private learning utilities and are
marked noindex; do not place an AdSense script in a shared base template or
inject Auto ads on those screens.

Set these environment variables on the production server:

    	ADSENSE_CLIENT_ID=ca-pub-your-publisher-id
    	ADSENSE_HOME_SLOT=your-homepage-ad-unit-id

The homepage stays ad-free when either value is missing. Use the real values
from AdSense, deploy them as server environment variables, and verify the
homepage source after deployment. Ads can remain blank while Google reviews
the account or site.

Before requesting another review:

- Keep only original, useful exercises in each language dataset.
- Remove repeated or automatically generated practice variants.
- Check the homepage, privacy policy, terms, and contact page as logged-out
  visitors.
- Do not place ads on login, dashboard, puzzle, error, or redirect screens.
- Use AdSense page exclusions if account-level Auto ads are enabled.
